576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Measured latency appeared to increase from ~14.5 ms to over 60 ms during long sessions. Investigation showed that the cause was not network degradation, but clock drift between the Jetson and the server.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Limitation of the Previous Application:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E ( The original system used a custom NTP synchronization performed only once at startup. Because quartz oscillators continuously drift over time, synchronization error accumulated throughout the session, creating the illusion of increasing network latency)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Chrony as solution:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Chrony was adopted as the operating system time manager, continuously correcting clock drift in real time.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
